# What must never reach a wordpress.org download.
#
# ⚠️ EVERY ONE OF THESE WAS IN THE PLUGIN WHEN PLUGIN CHECK WAS FIRST RUN AGAINST IT,
# and between them they produced 41 of the 44 findings — including the only two errors.
# None of it is a bug in the plugin; all of it is a bug in what we were shipping.
#
#   bin/review-check.php  a developer CLI script. Plugin Check reads it as plugin code,
#                         so its bare top-level variables became "non-prefixed globals"
#                         and its echo of a local array became unescaped output.
#   .gitignore            "Hidden files are not permitted."
#   SUBMISSION.md
# ⚠️ README.md TOO, AND FOR THE SAME REASON SUBMISSION.md IS HERE: Plugin Check reports
# "Unexpected markdown file in plugin root." The repository's README is written for
# somebody reading the source on GitHub; readme.txt is the one wordpress.org renders.
# Two audiences, two files, and only one of them belongs in the download.
README.md
# The listing artwork. wordpress.org serves these from the repository's own assets/
# directory, NOT from the plugin — shipping them would put 55KB of PNG on every
# install to draw a page nobody sees from inside their dashboard.
assets         "Unexpected markdown file in plugin root."
#
# The distributed plugin is the six files that do the work, plus readme and licence.
.gitignore
.distignore
.git
bin
SUBMISSION.md
# The listing artwork. wordpress.org serves these from the repository's own assets/
# directory, NOT from the plugin — shipping them would put 55KB of PNG on every
# install to draw a page nobody sees from inside their dashboard.
assets
